# Normalise line endings so a repo authored on Windows builds on Linux.
#
# build.sh runs on Vercel and on GitHub Actions, both Linux. A shell script
# checked in with CRLF fails there with "bad interpreter: bash^M", so the
# line ending is forced to LF regardless of the contributor's platform or
# core.autocrlf setting. The same applies to the YAML and JSON the build
# tooling reads.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf

*.png binary
